{
  "name": "glide_fwd",
  "note": "(anim-rework S3 keys, real-world standard, keyed by hand; never traced) The glide forward, weapon drawn: short steps (about 36 cm), heel first and rolled to the toe, knees bent 20-30 deg through the stance to absorb each step so the pelvis stays level (the upper body a stable platform), feet close to the line under the hips (add 2.5); the trunk at the ready stance (pelvis 6, chest 4 deg), no more lean; the hips and chest square (a 1 deg pelvis yaw). Phase 0 is the left heel strike; keys 0-0.375 are mirrored. Legs, pelvis and trunk only: the arms are keyed neutral (hanging, elbows 10) because the weapon arms stay procedural (hand IK on the gun). Angles in degrees in the body frame (x right, y up, z forward): pitch about x (+ the top forward), yaw about y (+ turns right), roll about z (+ the right side up). Pelvis offsets in cm from the standing rest. Arms: flex (+ forward, in the chest frame), abd (+ out), elbow (+ bent), inward. Legs (the Blender preview and the track only: the game's feet come from the foot planner): flex (+ the knee forward), add (+ the foot in toward the midline), knee (+ bent), ankle (+ the toes up).",
